WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.369 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But here's one of
the fundamental things

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.303 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think people
need to understand

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.305
about what Liz Cheney is doing,

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
is, we have a
separation of powers.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
The legislative branch
writes the laws,

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.611 align:start size:84% position:16%
the executive branch
carries them out,

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.014
and the judiciary
makes decisions,

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.016
from criminal law
to criminal cases,

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:19.919
to deciding disputes
between neighbors.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.956
What this commission has
done is taken on the role

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.291
of all of them, but
most importantly,

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:29.596
this January 6th Commission
is acting as the prosecutor.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:33.400
They're presenting evidence to
themselves as the judiciary,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.669
and then they are going
to be making the decision

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start position:0%
as the jury, so they have
actually subsumed in themselves

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.676
all aspects of decision-making.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.712
They will decide what
evidence comes in,

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.248 align:start size:97% position:3%
and if it doesn't fit their
narrative, we'll never see it,

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.583
it'll never see
the light of day.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.119
(somber music)

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.799 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
