obviously, a small state,

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.643
but an important one,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.812
but for the people
that don't know you.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.115 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I appreciate
that opportunity.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.217 align:start size:88% position:13%
Yes, I was going to give
a bit more background

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.451
about who I was.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.587 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
It was a wonderful
event at Peter's home,

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.456 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and so many of the people
there had never met me before,

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.658
so I wanted to give them
just a bit of background

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.394
so that they knew who they
were supporting and why.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.063
We oftentimes focus on the fact

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.865
that I'm running
against Liz Cheney,

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I'm not just running
against Liz Cheney,

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.535
I'm running for Wyoming.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.704
I have deep, deep
roots in Wyoming.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.739 align:start size:88% position:13%
I, my great-grandfather
came to Wyoming

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:23.476 align:start size:88% position:13%
in 1879 on a cattle
trail north from Texas,

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:27.180
and he ended up ranching
there for many, many years,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.015
and so I have lots of cousins,

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:88% position:13%
I have a very large
family here in Wyoming,

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.420
and then I come from
a large family myself.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.624
When I was born, I was
my parents' fifth child.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.058
When they brought me
home from the hospital,

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.461
my oldest sister
was five years old

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.429
and they had just
bought a ranch,

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.232
they were over $200,000 in debt,

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:49.769
they had $35 in the
bank and it was 1962,

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.639
so we were land-rich,
I guess, you'd say,

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.274
but awfully cash-poor.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.608
I grew up on that ranch.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
I grew up fixing
fence and moving cows

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:01.181 align:start size:97% position:3%
and flipping bales and doing
whatever was necessary.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.716
We all learned to drive when
we were about four years old

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.786
because we helped our dad
when he was feeding cows.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.188
We were very actively involved

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:10.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
and our parents
ensured that we were,

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
and one of the things
that they always taught us

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.760
when we were growing up,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.095
and I know that this sounds
a bit strange to some people

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.897
who don't grow up in
that kind of a life,

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:21.301
but my parents always told us
that we had a responsibility

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.936
to keep ourselves alive.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
From the time we were
very, very young,

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.105
three and four years old,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.508
we were told, we had to
keep ourselves alive.

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.543
They didn't put a lot
of constraints on us.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:81% position:19%
We rode horseback,
we did things,

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.849 align:start position:0%
we would be gone from the house
for six, seven hours a day,

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.351
we played with snapping turtles,

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had a rattlesnake that
lived under the house

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.821
for a period of time,

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:45.024
we did a lot of things out
there, but we, but with that,

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:48.094
we had a lot of freedom, I
guess, is what I'm saying,

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:51.264
and so the flip side of
freedom is responsibility

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the flip side of
responsibility is freedom,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.401
and right now in this country,

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.704
that isn't really the way
that people view things,

00:03:57.704 --> 00:04:00.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think Thomas Sowell
recently said it best

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.742 align:start size:88% position:13%
when he said, people are
no longer responsible

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.911
for themselves, but
they're responsible

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.546
for what other people did,

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.781
even if it was a
hundred years ago,

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.017
and I think that that's where
we're heading in this country,

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I think it's a
really wrong approach,

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.921 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I think that that's
why my background

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:16.623
really helps me to understand

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.558
because that freedom
is incredibly important

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.426
and it's part of
why I'm running.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.662
So in terms of my background,

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.564 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm a water and natural
resource attorney,

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.499
I'm a constitutional attorney,

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:29.135 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've been practicing
law for almost 33 years,

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've been fighting for
and working for Wyoming

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.339
for a long, long time.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.907 align:start size:81% position:19%
I work and I fight
for the people

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.409
who put food on your table,

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:38.344
gas in your car or
roof over your head,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.779
and they pave your highways.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:43.016 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so I have the credentials,
I have the background,

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.652 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have the knowledge
about Wyoming

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:97% position:3%
to be an effective
Congresswoman for the state,

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:51.891
but also, you mentioned that
Wyoming is an important state,

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.526 align:start size:81% position:19%
it's an incredibly
important state

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.728
to the prosperity
of this country.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.964
We're the Saudi Arabia
of the United States.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.399
We're the largest coal producer,

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.601
we're the largest
trona producer,

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:04.504
we're one of the top oil and
gas producers in the nation.

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
We really are instrumental
in terms of ensuring

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.677
prosperity in this country,

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:14.047
and so that's why it is
so incredibly important

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:16.249 align:start size:84% position:16%
to have someone
with my background,

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:18.985 align:start size:97% position:3%
my history and my knowledge
running for this seat,

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.486
because I need to
do it for Wyoming,

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:22.889
and I also need to
do for our country.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.757
- You know, it's funny, you
