it's coming from our coal.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:16.322 align:start size:97% position:3%
So these are great people
and it is intergenerational.

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:17.890
It's interesting,
several years ago,

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
I took a tour of the trona
mines over in Wyoming,

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:24.363
and trona is a baking soda

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:27.567
and what you use to make flat
glass and that sort of thing,

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I took a tour of that
and the number of men

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:33.706 align:start size:88% position:13%
who followed their
mothers into the mines,

00:09:33.706 --> 00:09:35.508 align:start size:88% position:13%
or followed their
fathers into the mines.

00:09:35.508 --> 00:09:37.577
We don't often think of
women of being minors,

00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:39.645 align:start size:84% position:16%
but in Wyoming,
they absolutely are.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:42.315 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're the heavy
equipment operators.

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:45.051
They are very actively
involved in the industry,

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:47.186
and I love meeting
with folks like that.

00:09:47.186 --> 00:09:52.191 align:start position:0%
Up in Gillette, just absolutely
a wonderful area to visit.

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:54.327
You go up there and you can see

00:09:54.327 --> 00:09:56.462
the magnitude of what
we produce in Wyoming,

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:58.764 align:start size:84% position:16%
again, with our oil
and gas, with our CBM.

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:01.167
Cold bed methane was
something we produced

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:06.172 align:start size:97% position:3%
a lot of earlier this century,
and then also our coal.

00:10:06.906 --> 00:10:08.074
Same with ranchers.

00:10:08.074 --> 00:10:10.876 align:start size:88% position:13%
We're a very independent
people in Wyoming.

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:13.679
What we really want
is we want the right

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:16.415
and the ability to make the
decisions for ourselves.

00:10:16.415 --> 00:10:18.618 align:start size:97% position:3%
We don't need the government
telling us what to do.

00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:20.152 align:start size:84% position:16%
We don't need the
government telling us

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:21.821
to put mask on our kids.

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:24.290 line:0%
We look at what's going
on with the truckers

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.459 line:0%
in Canada and we support them.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:28.127 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Those are the
people who make sure

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:30.229 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
that you have canned goods
in your grocery store,

00:10:30.229 --> 00:10:32.264
that you have meat in
your grocery store.

00:10:32.264 --> 00:10:34.700 align:start size:97% position:3%
Everybody in this country
ought to be supporting them,

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.769
and if this hadn't
become so political

00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:40.840 align:start size:84% position:16%
over all of the
coronavirus hysteria,

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.475
we all would be supporting them

00:10:42.475 --> 00:10:44.410 align:start size:88% position:13%
because they're standing
up for what's right,

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.078
they're standing up
for independence,

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:47.613
they're standing
up for all of us.

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:49.615 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I'm very, very
proud of them.

00:10:49.615 --> 00:10:51.684
I'm proud of the folks
in the United States

00:10:51.684 --> 00:10:53.085
who are doing the same thing.

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:54.720
I have a nephew who's trying

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.288 align:start size:81% position:19%
to get into the
tracking business,

00:10:56.288 --> 00:11:00.092 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's now purchased
two 18-wheelers,

00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:03.462 align:start position:0%
